@@ -9,6 +9,29 @@ You are welcome -- and encouraged -- to modify Fizzy to your liking.
 Please see our [Development guide](docs/development.md) for how to get Fizzy set up for local development.
 
 
+## Deploying to one server
+
+The included [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) configuration is for a single Linux server running Docker. It runs Fizzy, SQLite, local file storage, Action Cable, the cache, and Solid Queue in one application container. Kamal's proxy provides HTTPS through Let's Encrypt and SQLite databases and uploaded files are kept in the persistent `fizzy_storage` Docker volume.
+
+1. Point your hostname at the server and allow SSH plus ports 80 and 443. In `config/deploy.yml`, replace `fizzy.example.com` once in the `x-fizzy-host` value. Adjust `builder.arch` to `arm64` if the server is ARM-based. If SSH is not available as `root`, add your user under `ssh` as described by Kamal.
+2. Replace the SMTP values in the same file (`SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_DOMAIN`, `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`, and the port/authentication/TLS options). The default settings use authenticated SMTP on port 587 with STARTTLS.
+3. From a machine with Ruby and Docker running, install the bundle, copy the secrets template, and fill it with a stable `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, SMTP credentials, and a VAPID key pair:
+
+   ```sh
+   bundle install
+   cp .kamal/secrets.example .kamal/secrets
+   bin/rails secret # generate SECRET_KEY_BASE once
+   bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"'
+   ```
+
+4. Start the first deploy:
+
+   ```sh
+   bin/kamal setup
+   ```
+
+Visit `https://your-hostname` and sign up; the sign-in code is sent through the configured mail server. Later deploys use the same named volume, so they retain all application data and uploaded files. Background jobs and recurring tasks run alongside Puma inside the web container (`SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA=true`). Keep `.kamal/secrets` and back up the `fizzy_storage` volume independently of container deploys.
+
 ## Contributing
 
 We welcome contributions! Please read our [style guide](STYLE.md) before submitting code.
diff --git a/config/deploy.yml b/config/deploy.yml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0e4ce33
--- /dev/null
+++ b/config/deploy.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Replace this one value with the hostname that points to your server.
+x-fizzy-host: &fizzy-host fizzy.example.com
+
+service: fizzy
+image: fizzy
+
+servers:
+  web:
+    - *fizzy-host
+
+proxy:
+  ssl: true
+  host: *fizzy-host
+  app_port: 80
+
+# Use Kamal's local registry so an external registry account is not required.
+registry:
+  server: localhost:5555
+
+builder:
+  arch: amd64
+
+env:
+  clear:
+    RAILS_ENV: production
+    DATABASE_ADAPTER: sqlite
+    ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE: local
+    APP_FQDN: *fizzy-host
+    MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS: "Fizzy <fizzy@example.com>"
+    SMTP_ADDRESS: smtp.example.com
+    SMTP_DOMAIN: *fizzy-host
+    SMTP_PORT: "587"
+    SMTP_AUTHENTICATION: plain
+    SMTP_TLS: "false"
+    SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO: "true"
+    SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA: "true"
+    WEB_CONCURRENCY: "1"
+    JOB_CONCURRENCY: "1"
+  secret:
+    - SECRET_KEY_BASE
+    - SMTP_USERNAME
+    - SMTP_PASSWORD
+    - VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY
+    - VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY
+
+volumes:
+  - fizzy_storage:/rails/storage
+
+asset_path: /rails/public/assets
+
+aliases:
+  console: app exec --interactive --reuse "bin/rails console"
+  shell: app exec --interactive --reuse "bash"
